 succeeded in 0ms:
46:| 19 | `agent_runs` | `kind` enum (morning_brief, eod, sunday_review), `status`, `degraded` bool (ran with expired token / stale data), `started_at`, `finished_at`, `tool_turns`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `estimated_cost`, `output_markdown`, `error`, `model` | yes |
47:| 20 | `tool_calls` | `agent_run_id` (nullable), `transport` enum (mcp, scheduled), `tool_name`, `arguments` jsonb, `duration_ms`, `error`, `created_at`. This is where MCP and runtime tool telemetry goes, not `audit_events`. | yes |
80:| `Jobs::FailureDigestJob` | daily 17:00 | One email listing failed `sync_runs`, `agent_runs`, and Solid Queue failed executions since the last digest, grouped by kind |
81:| `Memory::PullRepoJob` | every 30 min | `git -C $MEMORY_REPO_PATH pull --ff-only`; record `sync_runs` |
82:| `Agent::MorningBriefJob` | 07:00 market days | See §3 |
112:Every call writes a `tool_calls` row. Nothing in this section writes to `audit_events`.
114:**MCP server (revised after the step 8 counselors review).** `McpController < ActionController::API` at `match "/mcp", via: [post, get, delete]`: a `before_action` checks the bearer (presence and byte length before `secure_compare`; never logged) and answers 401 with `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="invalid_token"` and a one-line JSON body, no HTML page and no `resource_metadata` (that would send Claude looking for an authorization server that does not exist). The action builds `MCP::Server` from the registry and hands the request to the gem's `StreamableHTTPTransport` with `stateless: true`, `enable_json_response: true`, `serve_subscriptions_listen: false`, `allowed_hosts` from `config.hosts` (the gem's DNS-rebinding guard rejects everything but loopback by default), and `max_request_bytes` well under the 4 MiB default; the transport handles GET, DELETE, the protocol-version header, notifications (202), and both the 2025 handshake and the 2026-07-28 stateless transport. Rails `rate_limit to: 60, within: 1.minute` on the controller; JSON only; no CORS. Tools return `MCP::Tool::Response` with `structured_content` plus a text block of the same JSON, `additionalProperties: false` on every schema, `output_schema` declared, and annotations `read_only_hint: true, destructive_hint: false, idempotent_hint: true, open_world_hint: false`. Tool exceptions never reach the transport: one dispatch wrapper rescues, writes the `tool_calls` row in an `ensure`, and returns a tool error carrying only the Schwab error message. Quotes and price history are cached with a long expiry and their own `fetched_at`; age beyond the freshness window triggers a refetch and a failed refetch returns the old entry with `stale: true`; the tools draw on a 70/min share of the Schwab budget so a chatty session cannot starve sync, and a rate limit is a tool error with `retry_after`, never a sleep. `get_portfolio` and `get_account_health` wrap the `Dashboard` read model rather than re-deriving anything; outputs carry the `protection` enum, nil for unknown risk, decimal strings for money, ISO 8601 New York timestamps, and never a `raw` column, an account hash, or the user's email (accounts are labelled by role). `get_journal` paginates (`limit` 50 default, 200 max, `offset`, `include_legs` off by default); `get_quotes` takes at most 50 symbols and reports `invalid_symbols`; `get_price_history` takes an enum range mapped to daily or weekly candles; `get_risk_rules` returns an empty list with `available: false` so the agent does not infer missing data. A spec walks every tool's serialized output for the account-hash pattern and `accountNumber`.
118:**Scheduled runtime:** `Agent::Run` wraps one Messages API conversation: system prompt = memory repo markdown files + setup stats + token health + as-of timestamps; tools = scheduled-allowed registry; hard cap `MAX_TOOL_TURNS = 12`; result stored in `agent_runs` and emailed via `BriefMailer`. Prompts live in `app/models/agent/prompts/*.md.erb`. The morning-brief prompt states that earnings and economic-calendar data are unavailable in Phase 1 and must not be inferred. Morning brief and EOD are real; Sunday review stub does not call the API.
228:9. Scheduled runtime + mailers (briefs, nags, failure digest) + memory repo pull.

