docs/phase-1-plan.md:44:| 17 | `market_days` | `date` (unique), `trading` bool, `session_opens_at` (pre-market), `regular_opens_at`, `regular_closes_at`, `session_closes_at` (post-market), `raw` jsonb, `fetched_at`, `source` enum (schwab, fallback) | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:45:| 18 | `sync_runs` | `feed` enum (accounts, positions, orders, activities, market_hours, memory_repo, snapshots; balances ride with positions), `account_id` (nullable; cursors are per account and feed), `status` (running, succeeded, partial, failed, skipped_token), `started_at`, `finished_at`, `error`, `records_touched`, `unmapped_values` jsonb, `window_from`, `window_to` (captured before the request; the next window starts from it), `gap_from` (set when the computed window start is later than the last success: data Schwab can no longer return) | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:46:| 19 | `agent_runs` | `kind` enum (morning_brief, eod, sunday_review), `status`, `degraded` bool (ran with expired token / stale data), `started_at`, `finished_at`, `tool_turns`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `estimated_cost`, `output_markdown`, `error`, `model` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:47:| 20 | `tool_calls` | `agent_run_id` (nullable), `transport` enum (mcp, scheduled), `tool_name`, `arguments` jsonb, `duration_ms`, `error`, `created_at`. This is where MCP and runtime tool telemetry goes, not `audit_events`. | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:60:**Token gating.** Only `Sync::TickJob` and the agent jobs are scheduled; everything else is enqueued by them. When `SchwabToken.current` is not usable, the tick job writes one `sync_runs` `skipped_token` row per hour, audits `sync_paused_token_expired` once per episode, and enqueues nothing. No self-re-enqueue, so the queue cannot grow. The re-auth callback (`issue!`) clears the pause, audits `sync_resumed`, and enqueues `Sync::CatchUpJob`, which runs all feeds with windows widened to cover the gap (capped at the 60-day limit). Agent jobs run degraded rather than wait: `degraded: true`, the prompt states the token is unusable and every number carries its as-of time, the email subject is prefixed, and the token status line sits at the top of every brief so a dead nag path is still visible daily. Snapshots are not written for days without a fresh balance.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:64:**Health and nags.** `Schwab::TokenHealthJob` runs 08:00 and 20:00 ET. Nag when: no usable token (absent, revoked, or expired), sent at every run; or the 24-hour warning, sent once per token row (deduped on token id in the audit data). Monday/Tuesday escalation fires when `SchwabToken.current.issued_at` is before the most recent Sunday 18:00 ET, which is the PRD's literal "the Sunday re-auth hasn't happened"; no buffer, no comparison against the coming Sunday. Cron strings carry `America/New_York` explicitly. The refresh task gets a higher queue priority than sync.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:70:| `Sync::TickJob` | every 5 min | Sole scheduled sync entry point. Refreshes `market_days` for today (New York) plus 7 days when missing or `source: fallback` (one call per date; a market-hours failure never aborts the tick). Due checks compare against the last *started* run per account and feed with 1-minute slack, and a `running` run is never due; jobs also declare Solid Queue `limits_concurrency` keyed on account and feed so backlog cannot double-enqueue. Cadences apply to trading-enabled accounts: positions (15 min inside the session window pre-market through post-market, 60 min otherwise), orders and activities (5 min inside, 60 outside); read-only accounts sync hourly. `Snapshots::DailyJob` once per market day after `regular_closes_at` + 20 min, only when that day's calendar row came from Schwab. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:80:| `Jobs::FailureDigestJob` | daily 17:00 | One email listing failed `sync_runs`, `agent_runs`, and Solid Queue failed executions since the last digest, grouped by kind |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:81:| `Memory::PullRepoJob` | every 30 min | `git -C $MEMORY_REPO_PATH pull --ff-only`; record `sync_runs` |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:84:| `Agent::SundayReviewJob` | Sunday 18:00 | Phase 1 stub, no API call: re-auth link, token age, sync health, job failures, setup stats table |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:112:Every call writes a `tool_calls` row. Nothing in this section writes to `audit_events`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:114:**MCP server (revised after the step 8 counselors review).** `McpController < ActionController::API` at `match "/mcp", via: [post, get, delete]`: a `before_action` checks the bearer (presence and byte length before `secure_compare`; never logged) and answers 401 with `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="invalid_token"` and a one-line JSON body, no HTML page and no `resource_metadata` (that would send Claude looking for an authorization server that does not exist). The action builds `MCP::Server` from the registry and hands the request to the gem's `StreamableHTTPTransport` with `stateless: true`, `enable_json_response: true`, `serve_subscriptions_listen: false`, `allowed_hosts` from `config.hosts` (the gem's DNS-rebinding guard rejects everything but loopback by default), and `max_request_bytes` well under the 4 MiB default; the transport handles GET, DELETE, the protocol-version header, notifications (202), and both the 2025 handshake and the 2026-07-28 stateless transport. Rails `rate_limit to: 60, within: 1.minute` on the controller; JSON only; no CORS. Tools return `MCP::Tool::Response` with `structured_content` plus a text block of the same JSON, `additionalProperties: false` on every schema, `output_schema` declared, and annotations `read_only_hint: true, destructive_hint: false, idempotent_hint: true, open_world_hint: false`. Tool exceptions never reach the transport: one dispatch wrapper rescues, writes the `tool_calls` row in an `ensure`, and returns a tool error carrying only the Schwab error message. Quotes and price history are cached with a long expiry and their own `fetched_at`; age beyond the freshness window triggers a refetch and a failed refetch returns the old entry with `stale: true`; the tools draw on a 70/min share of the Schwab budget so a chatty session cannot starve sync, and a rate limit is a tool error with `retry_after`, never a sleep. `get_portfolio` and `get_account_health` wrap the `Dashboard` read model rather than re-deriving anything; outputs carry the `protection` enum, nil for unknown risk, decimal strings for money, ISO 8601 New York timestamps, and never a `raw` column, an account hash, or the user's email (accounts are labelled by role). `get_journal` paginates (`limit` 50 default, 200 max, `offset`, `include_legs` off by default); `get_quotes` takes at most 50 symbols and reports `invalid_symbols`; `get_price_history` takes an enum range mapped to daily or weekly candles; `get_risk_rules` returns an empty list with `available: false` so the agent does not infer missing data. A spec walks every tool's serialized output for the account-hash pattern and `accountNumber`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:118:**Scheduled runtime:** `Agent::Run` wraps one Messages API conversation: system prompt = memory repo markdown files + setup stats + token health + as-of timestamps; tools = scheduled-allowed registry; hard cap `MAX_TOOL_TURNS = 12`; result stored in `agent_runs` and emailed via `BriefMailer`. Prompts live in `app/models/agent/prompts/*.md.erb`. The morning-brief prompt states that earnings and economic-calendar data are unavailable in Phase 1 and must not be inferred. Morning brief and EOD are real; Sunday review stub does not call the API.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:172:Dashboard day change is flow-adjusted (equity − flows − prior snapshot equity) and reads "no prior snapshot" on a gap day. The EOD fills recap reads activities journaled today; the missing-post-mortem list excludes `needs_review` and `excluded_from_stats` trades.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:180:**Model prerequisites built in this step.** `SchwabToken.status` (missing, revoked, expired, expiring, healthy; the Monday/Tuesday missed-Sunday nag stays in the health job) extracted from the health job and used by the banner, the system page, the mailer, and later `get_account_health`; `Account#sync_interval(feed)` and `Account#last_sync(feed)` extracted from the tick so views and scheduler cannot disagree; `trades.review_deferred_at` so Skip is durable ("later, not never": queue ordered by priority, then deferred-at nulls first, then oldest); `Position#distance_to_stop` guarded on a stop price rather than full protection so a partially covered stop still shows its distance; CASH_EQUIVALENT positions skipped by the positions sync so the sweep fund is neither a position nor a trade; `trading_enabled` requires `taxable`; an `account_configured` audit kind and an immediate sync enqueue when an account is enabled; setups creatable by name from the review form.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:184:| Dashboard | `/` | Banner by state: not connected (connect CTA); revoked (re-auth, with the refresh error); expired (re-auth, "sync paused since" from the first skipped run); expiring (re-auth, "Sunday's email will remind you" when covered); halted ("Halted by John, Mon 11:14a: reason. Clear it on the System page", no fake rule copy, re-auth link still shown if sync is also down); sync failed with a usable token (one-line status under the header, not a banner); needs setup (link to the accounts section). Equity with flow-adjusted change since the prior snapshot by date ("since Fri close" on a Monday, "first snapshot after today's close" before one exists); settled and unsettled cash ("unavailable", never zero, when both readings are nil); open risk labelled as known protected risk plus "N excluded: partial / oversized / awaiting / trailing / no stop"; positions as a list of rows sorted unprotected, awaiting, and trailing first then ascending distance, each with symbol, size, distance to stop as the primary number, the protection state inline, unrealized P&L (market value minus cost basis) second, and the older of the positions and orders as-of stamps; "N trades need review" callout; "Proposals: Phase 2" without a link; empty states for not connected, waiting for the first sync, and no open positions. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:186:| Trade detail / post-mortem | `/trades`, `/trades/:id` | List with needs-review and missing-post-mortem filters (the EOD email deep-links there); detail with legs, planned versus actual stop (working stop for open trades, closing price when stopped out), R; the Flow 4 quick entry: required one line plus followed or improvised |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:187:| System | `/system` | Token status and age against 7 days with next Sunday 18:00 marked and a loud line when the token dies before it; last success and latest status per feed per account, `gap_from` when set, pause reason and since; failed sync runs plus Solid Queue failed executions in 7 days; shadow mode as a read-only indicator; API spend rendered as "0 runs, briefs start in step 9"; memory repo "never"; accounts table showing each account's equity and top symbols with an inline form for nickname, type, and enabled. Halt: set requires a reason and audits `manual_halt_set`; clear requires typed confirmation checked server-side and audits `manual_halt_cleared`. One word everywhere: Halt. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:224:5. Sync jobs, market calendar, tick scheduler, `sync_runs`, working-stop detection.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:228:9. Scheduled runtime + mailers (briefs, nags, failure digest) + memory repo pull.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:16:8. **Mappers never crash a sync.** Unknown enum values are stored raw and mapped to `unknown`/`other`; missing optional fields are nil; a record that cannot be identified is quarantined with its raw JSON and counted on the `sync_runs` row, and the run finishes `partial`.
